  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">function</span> E2EErrorHandler <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CM_10470\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">[SWS_CM_10470]</a></span> <span class=\"ups\">Upstream: <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00401\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00401</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00402\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00402</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">virtual void E2EErrorHandler (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"../namespaces/ns_com_ara_com_e2e_f19464.html#SWS_CM_10474\">ara::com::e2e::ComE2EErrc</a> errorCode, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"../namespaces/ns_com_ara_com_e2e_f19464.html\">ara::com::e2e::DataID</a> dataID, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"../namespaces/ns_com_ara_com_e2e_f19464.html\">ara::com::e2e::MessageCounter</a> message Counter);</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Implementation may be overridden by the actual ServiceSkeleton implementation and it is not required to be reentrant. If the E2E error is a CRC error then some parts of the received message are faulty. If this part is the DataID then the E2E error handler is called with a faulty DataID. Consequently, in case of CRC error the server application can not rely on the DataID received by its error handler.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n\n"
  },
